---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const sections = [['scope','Scope'],['collect','Information collected'],['use','How information is used'],['forms','Forms & third parties'],['sharing','Sharing'],['retention','Retention & security'],['rights','Your choices'],['international','International use'],['updates','Updates & contact']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Web Grouth" description="How Web Grouth collects, uses, stores and protects information submitted through website forms, email and WhatsApp.">
  <div class="saas-page">
    <section class="saas-hero"><div class="shell saas-hero-grid"><div class="saas-hero-copy" data-reveal><div class="saas-breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy</span></div><span class="saas-kicker">Privacy policy</span><h1>Your campaign information should stay <span>purpose-limited.</span></h1><p>This policy explains what Web Grouth receives through the website and direct communication, why it is used and the choices available to you.</p></div><aside class="saas-hero-panel" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1"><span>Policy summary</span><ul><li>Effective date <span>31 August 2026</span></li><li>Data controller <span>Web Grouth</span></li><li>Website <span>webgrouth.com</span></li><li>Privacy contact <span>nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com</span></li></ul></aside></div></section>
    <section class="saas-section"><div class="shell legal-layout">
      <aside class="legal-toc"><strong>On this page</strong><nav>{sections.map(([id,label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav></aside>
      <article class="legal-content">
        <p class="legal-note">Web Grouth collects only the information reasonably needed to answer enquiries, evaluate orders, deliver agreed services and maintain business records. Do not submit passwords, private access keys or unrelated sensitive information through website forms.</p>
        <section id="scope"><h2>1. Scope</h2><p>This Privacy Policy applies to information submitted through Webgrouth.com, the order and contact forms, email, WhatsApp and direct business communication with Web Grouth. It does not control the independent privacy practices of publishers, search engines or other third-party websites.</p></section>
        <section id="collect"><h2>2. Information we collect</h2><p>Depending on how you contact Web Grouth, the following information may be received:</p><ul><li>Name, business email, telephone or WhatsApp number.</li><li>Company, client website and target page information.</li><li>Niche, anchor text, keywords, content topics, budget and publisher preferences.</li><li>Messages, approvals, order history, invoices and payment records.</li><li>Basic technical information made available by hosting or security systems, such as IP address, browser type, referring page and request time.</li></ul><p>The website does not ask for card details. Any payment method is arranged separately under the confirmed order terms.</p></section>
        <section id="use"><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to respond to enquiries, assess campaign eligibility, prepare publisher options, fulfil approved placements, provide support, maintain records, prevent abuse and comply with applicable obligations.</p><p>Web Grouth may also use aggregated or non-identifying information to improve website usability and internal campaign workflows. Personal information is not sold.</p></section>
        <section id="forms"><h2>4. Website forms and communication providers</h2><p>Website forms use FormSubmit to forward submitted information to the Web Grouth email inbox. FormSubmit processes the submission for delivery. You should review its applicable privacy terms before submitting if this processing is a concern.</p><p>If you choose email, WhatsApp or telephone contact, the relevant provider processes communication under its own policies. Links to third-party websites do not mean Web Grouth controls their privacy or security.</p><h3>Cookies and local storage</h3><p>The current website does not require an account and does not intentionally place advertising cookies. Essential hosting, security or performance systems may process basic request information. If analytics or additional cookies are introduced, this policy and any required consent controls should be updated.</p></section>
        <section id="sharing"><h2>5. When information may be shared</h2><p>Information is shared only when reasonably necessary for the service, such as with a selected publisher, writer, operational service provider or professional adviser. Only relevant campaign details should be shared with a publisher; unnecessary client contact information is not required for routine placement.</p><p>Information may also be disclosed when required by law, to protect legal rights or security, or in connection with a legitimate business reorganisation subject to appropriate safeguards.</p></section>
        <section id="retention"><h2>6. Retention and security</h2><p>Enquiry and business records are kept only as long as reasonably needed for communication, fulfilment, accounting, dispute handling, fraud prevention and legal obligations. Retention periods may vary based on the nature of the order and applicable requirements.</p><p>Reasonable administrative and technical steps are used to protect information. However, no internet transmission, email or third-party service can be guaranteed completely secure.</p></section>
        <section id="rights"><h2>7. Your choices and requests</h2><p>Subject to applicable law and necessary record-keeping, you may ask Web Grouth to:</p><ul><li>Confirm whether your personal information is held.</li><li>Correct inaccurate contact or campaign information.</li><li>Delete information that is no longer required.</li><li>Object to or restrict certain uses.</li><li>Stop non-essential marketing communication.</li></ul><p>A request may require reasonable identity verification. Some information may be retained where necessary for payment, legal, security or dispute records.</p></section>
        <section id="international"><h2>8. International service</h2><p>Web Grouth serves clients and works with publishers in multiple countries. Information may therefore be processed or communicated across borders where providers, publishers or campaign participants are located. Appropriate purpose limitation should be applied to each transfer.</p><p>The services are intended for business users and are not directed to children.</p></section>
        <section id="updates"><h2>9. Policy updates and contact</h2><p>This policy may change when website forms, service providers or business practices change. The effective date identifies the current version.</p><p>Privacy questions or requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com">nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com</a>, through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, or by WhatsApp at <a href="https://wa.me/923327810261">+92 332 7810261</a>.</p></section>
      </article>
    </div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
